{"id":"abb49d8e5ad3efa90c4d29ad1823f5a47bede709","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"abb49d8e5ad3efa90c4d29ad1823f5a47bede709","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/systemd-firstboot.xml","lines":["@@ -127,6 +127,53 @@","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v246\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><option>--addon=<replaceable>NAME</replaceable></option></term>","+        <listitem><para>Takes an addon name. Instead of applying the settings to the file system in the disk","+        image specified with <option>--image=</option>, write them as a","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-stub</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+        addon <filename>loader/addons/<replaceable>NAME</replaceable>.addon.efi</filename> into the boot","+        partition of the image, replacing an addon of the same name. That is the partition the stub loads","+        addons from, i.e. the XBOOTLDR partition if the image has one, and the EFI System Partition","+        otherwise. This allows customizing an image","+        whose root file system is signed and hence cannot be modified. The settings are converted into the","+        system credentials of the same meaning (see the Credentials section below, plus","+        <varname>system.machine_id</varname> for the machine ID), packed into a cpio archive and carried in","+        the <literal>.initrd</literal> section of the addon, from where the stub passes them on to the","+        system. A kernel command line specified with <option>--kernel-command-line=</option> is carried in","+        the <literal>.cmdline</literal> section. The image is not mounted for this, its partition table is","+        read and the file is placed in the boot partition with","+        <citerefentry project='mankier'><refentrytitle>mtools</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>.","+        For this mode of operation the image must be a regular file, block devices are not supported. The","+        addon is built from the stub for the architecture of the host, for images of a different","+        architecture point <varname>$SYSTEMD_ADDON_STUB</varname> to the matching stub.","+        The addon is not signed; whether the stub loads it is subject to the Secure Boot policy of the","+        system, see <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-stub</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.","+        Cannot be combined with the <option>--prompt*</option>, <option>--copy*</option>,","+        <option>--reset</option>, <option>--force</option> and <option>--delete-root-password</option>","+        switches, as those operate on the file system tree of the image. The addon is built from","+        <filename>/usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi/addon<replaceable>ARCH</replaceable>.efi.stub</filename>, the","+        <varname>$SYSTEMD_ADDON_STUB</varname> environment variable may be set to use a different stub.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><option>--key=<replaceable>KEYRING</replaceable>:<optional><replaceable>NAME</replaceable>=</optional><replaceable>PATH</replaceable></option></term>","+        <listitem><para>Provisions a PEM-encoded X.509 certificate for one of the kernel keyrings","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-keyring-setup.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+        manages, for example to verify extension images with, as part of the addon written with","+        <option>--addon=</option>. <replaceable>KEYRING</replaceable> is one of <literal>dm-verity</literal>,","+        <literal>fs-verity</literal> and <literal>bpf</literal>. The file is included as credential","+        <varname>keyring-setup.<replaceable>KEYRING</replaceable>.<replaceable>NAME</replaceable></varname>,","+        with <replaceable>NAME</replaceable> defaulting to the file name without its suffix. It must consist","+        of lowercase letters, digits, <literal>.</literal>, <literal>_</literal> and <literal>-</literal>. A","+        <literal>=</literal> is only taken as the separator if it precedes any <literal>/</literal> in the","+        argument. May be used multiple times.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","       <varlistentry>","         <term><option>--locale=<replaceable>LOCALE</replaceable></option></term>","         <term><option>--locale-messages=<replaceable>LOCALE</replaceable></option></term>"],"additions":47,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"mkosi/mkosi.sanitizers/mkosi.postinst","lines":["@@ -98,6 +98,8 @@ wrap=(","     multipath","     multipathd","     nvme","+    objcopy","+    objdump","     p11-kit","     pkill","     ps"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/firstboot/firstboot.c","lines":["@@ -22,16 +22,20 @@"," #include \"creds-util.h\""," #include \"dissect-image.h\""," #include \"dlopen-note.h\"","+#include \"efi-loader.h\""," #include \"env-file.h\""," #include \"errno-util.h\""," #include \"fd-util.h\""," #include \"fileio.h\""," #include \"firstboot-util.h\"","+#include \"format-util.h\""," #include \"fs-util.h\""," #include \"glyph-util.h\""," #include \"hostname-setup.h\""," #include \"hostname-util.h\""," #include \"image-policy.h\"","+#include \"initrd-cpio.h\"","+#include \"iovec-util.h\""," #include \"kbd-util.h\""," #include \"label-util.h\""," #include \"libcrypt-util.h\"","@@ -39,6 +43,7 @@"," #include \"locale-util.h\""," #include \"lock-util.h\""," #include \"loop-util.h\"","+#include \"machine-credential.h\""," #include \"machine-tags.h\""," #include \"main-func.h\""," #include \"memory-util.h\"","@@ -47,6 +52,7 @@"," #include \"parse-argument.h\""," #include \"password-quality-util.h\""," #include \"path-util.h\"","+#include \"pe-addon.h\""," #include \"plymouth-util.h\""," #include \"prompt-util.h\""," #include \"runtime-scope.h\"","@@ -60,6 +66,8 @@"," #include \"user-util.h\""," #include \"vconsole-util.h\""," #include \"verbs.h\"","+#include \"vfat-util.h\"","+#include \"voa-util.h\""," "," static char *arg_root = NULL;"," static char *arg_image = NULL;","@@ -95,6 +103,8 @@ static ImagePolicy *arg_image_policy = NULL;"," static bool arg_chrome = true;"," static bool arg_mute_console = false;"," static LabelContext *arg_label_context = NULL;","+static char *arg_addon = NULL;","+static MachineCredentialContext arg_keys = {};"," "," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_root, freep);"," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_image, freep);","@@ -109,6 +119,8 @@ STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_root_shell, freep);"," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_kernel_cmdline, freep);"," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_image_policy, image_policy_freep);"," STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_label_context, mac_label_context_freep);","+STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_addon, freep);","+STATIC_DESTRUCTOR_REGISTER(arg_keys, machine_credential_context_done);"," "," COMMAND(","         \"systemd-firstboot\\0\",","@@ -1411,6 +1423,255 @@ static int process_reset(int rfd) {","         return 0;"," }"," ","+static int parse_key_argument(const char *s) {","+        int r;","+","+        assert(s);","+","+        /* Takes \"KEYRING:[NAME=]PATH\". The certificate in the file becomes the credential","+         * \"keyring-setup.KEYRING.NAME\", which systemd-keyring-setup enrolls into the kernel keyring at boot,","+         * with NAME defaulting to the file name without its suffix. */","+","+        const char *e = strchr(s, ':');","+        if (!e)","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Missing keyring in '%s', expected KEYRING:[NAME=]PATH.\", s);","+","+        _cleanup_free_ char *keyring = strndup(s, e - s);","+        if (!keyring)","+                return log_oom();","+        if (!STR_IN_SET(keyring, \"dm-verity\", \"fs-verity\", \"bpf\"))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Unknown keyring '%s', expected dm-verity, fs-verity or bpf.\", keyring);","+","+        /* A '=' only separates the name if it comes before any '/', so that a path containing '=' can be","+         * passed without a name */","+        _cleanup_free_ char *name = NULL, *path = NULL;","+        const char *k = e + 1, *eq = strchr(k, '='), *slash = strchr(k, '/');","+        if (eq && (!slash || eq < slash)) {","+                name = strndup(k, eq - k);","+                path = strdup(eq + 1);","+        } else {","+                _cleanup_free_ char *fn = NULL;","+                r = path_extract_filename(k, &fn);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to extract file name from '%s': %m\", k);","+","+                char *dot = strrchr(fn, '.');","+                if (dot && dot != fn)","+                        *dot = 0;","+","+                name = TAKE_PTR(fn);","+                path = strdup(k);","+        }","+        if (!name || !path)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        if (isempty(path))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Missing key file path in '%s'.\", s);","+        if (isempty(name) || name[0] == '.')","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Missing key name in '%s'.\", s);","+        if (!voa_identifier_is_valid(name, /* allow_colon= */ false))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Invalid key name '%s', expected lowercase letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-'.\", name);","+","+        _cleanup_free_ char *id = strjoin(\"keyring-setup.\", keyring, \".\", name);","+        if (!id)","+                return log_oom();","+        if (!credential_name_valid(id))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Invalid key name '%s'.\", name);","+","+        /* The file is read securely as it might not be a public key after all, and with the limit the","+         * credential has at boot, rather than silently cut off there */","+        _cleanup_(erase_and_freep) char *data = NULL;","+        size_t size;","+        r = read_full_file_full(","+                        AT_FDCWD, path,","+                        /* offset= */ UINT64_MAX,","+                        CREDENTIAL_SIZE_MAX,","+                        READ_FULL_FILE_SECURE|READ_FULL_FILE_FAIL_WHEN_LARGER,","+                        /* bind_name= */ NULL,","+                        &data, &size);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to read key file '%s': %m\", path);","+        if (size == 0)","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(ENODATA), \"Key file '%s' is empty.\", path);","+","+        r = machine_credential_add(&arg_keys, id, data, size);","+        if (r == -EEXIST)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Key '%s' specified more than once.\", name);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to add key '%s': %m\", name);","+","+        return 0;","+}","+","+static int addon_add_credential(MachineCredentialContext *creds, const char *id, const char *value) {","+        int r;","+","+        assert(creds);","+        assert(id);","+","+        if (!value)","+                return 0;","+","+        r = machine_credential_add(creds, id, value, SIZE_MAX);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to add credential '%s': %m\", id);","+","+        log_debug(\"Added credential '%s' to addon.\", id);","+        return 1;","+}","+","+static int write_addon(void) {","+        _cleanup_(machine_credential_context_done) MachineCredentialContext creds = {};","+        int r;","+","+        assert(arg_addon);","+        assert(arg_image);","+","+        /* Instead of applying the settings to the image, turn them into the credentials systemd-firstboot","+         * (and PID 1, for the machine ID) consume at boot, pack them into a cpio that an initrd addon","+         * carries, and drop that addon into the ESP of the image, so that it customizes an otherwise","+         * immutable image. The kernel command line goes into the addon as such. */","+","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.locale\", arg_locale);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.locale-messages\", arg_locale_messages);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.keymap\", arg_keymap);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.timezone\", arg_timezone);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.hostname\", arg_hostname);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        if (arg_machine_tags) {","+                _cleanup_free_ char *tags = strv_join(arg_machine_tags, \":\");","+                if (!tags)","+                        return log_oom();","+","+                r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"firstboot.machine-tags\", tags);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return r;","+        }","+","+        if (arg_root_password) {","+                /* Never ship the plaintext password, hash it here if needed */","+                _cleanup_(erase_and_freep) char *hashed = NULL;","+                const char *p = arg_root_password;","+","+                if (!arg_root_password_is_hashed) {","+                        r = hash_password(arg_root_password, &hashed);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to hash password: %m\");","+                        p = hashed;","+                }","+","+                r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"passwd.hashed-password.root\", p);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return r;","+        }","+","+        r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"passwd.shell.root\", arg_root_shell);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        if (!sd_id128_is_null(arg_machine_id)) {","+                r = addon_add_credential(&creds, \"system.machine_id\", SD_ID128_TO_STRING(arg_machine_id));","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return r;","+        }","+","+        FOREACH_ARRAY(k, arg_keys.credentials, arg_keys.n_credentials) {","+                r = machine_credential_add(&creds, k->id, k->data, k->size);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to add key '%s': %m\", k->id);","+        }","+","+        if (creds.n_credentials == 0 && isempty(arg_kernel_cmdline))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"No settings specified, refusing to write an empty addon.\");","+","+        /* The credentials are subject to the same limit at boot, hence refuse what would be dropped there */","+        uint64_t total = 0;","+        FOREACH_ARRAY(k, creds.credentials, creds.n_credentials)","+                total += k->size;","+        if (total > CREDENTIALS_TOTAL_SIZE_MAX)","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(E2BIG), \"Credentials are %s in total, which exceeds the limit of %s.\",","+                                       FORMAT_BYTES(total), FORMAT_BYTES(CREDENTIALS_TOTAL_SIZE_MAX));","+","+        /* Serialize against other instances writing into the same image. An OFD lock, so that it cannot","+         * get into the way of mtools, should it take a BSD lock on the image itself. */","+        _cleanup_close_ int image_fd = xopenat(AT_FDCWD, arg_image, O_RDWR);","+        if (image_fd < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(image_fd, \"Failed to open image '%s': %m\", arg_image);","+","+        r = lock_generic(image_fd, LOCK_UNPOSIX, LOCK_EX);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to lock image '%s': %m\", arg_image);","+","+        _cleanup_(iovec_done_erase) struct iovec cpio = {};","+        if (creds.n_credentials > 0) {","+                r = initrd_cpio_credentials_to_memory(&creds, &cpio);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return r;","+        }","+","+        /* Find the partition the stub will look for addons on, without mounting anything: dissect the","+         * partition table only. The stub loads addons from the partition the UKI was loaded from, which is","+         * the XBOOTLDR partition if the image has one, and the ESP otherwise. */","+        _cleanup_(dissected_image_unrefp) DissectedImage *m = NULL;","+        r = dissect_image_file_and_warn(","+                        arg_image,","+                        /* verity= */ NULL,","+                        /* mount_options= */ NULL,","+                        arg_image_policy,","+                        /* filter= */ NULL,","+                        DISSECT_IMAGE_READ_ONLY|DISSECT_IMAGE_GPT_ONLY,","+                        &m);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+        PartitionDesignator boot = m->partitions[PARTITION_XBOOTLDR].found ? PARTITION_XBOOTLDR : PARTITION_ESP;","+        if (!m->partitions[boot].found)","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(ENXIO), \"Image '%s' has neither an XBOOTLDR partition nor an EFI System Partition.\", arg_image);","+","+        /* mtools wants paths, hence build the addon in a temporary file */","+        _cleanup_(unlink_and_freep) char *addon_path = NULL;","+        r = tempfn_random_child(/* p= */ NULL, \"addon\", &addon_path);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to generate temporary file name: %m\");","+","+        _cleanup_close_ int addon_fd = xopenat_full(AT_FDCWD, addon_path, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL, /* xopen_flags= */ 0, 0600);","+        if (addon_fd < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(addon_fd, \"Failed to create temporary file '%s': %m\", addon_path);","+","+        const char *stub = secure_getenv(\"SYSTEMD_ADDON_STUB\") ?: PE_ADDON_STUB_PATH;","+        r = pe_addon_make(stub, arg_kernel_cmdline, &cpio, addon_fd);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        uint64_t offset = m->partitions[boot].offset;","+","+        r = vfat_mkdir(arg_image, offset, \"loader/addons\");","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        _cleanup_free_ char *dest = strjoin(\"loader/addons/\", arg_addon, \".addon.efi\");","+        if (!dest)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        r = vfat_copy_file(arg_image, offset, addon_path, dest);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        log_info(\"Wrote addon '%s' with %zu credential%s to the %s of '%s'.\",","+                 dest, creds.n_credentials, creds.n_credentials == 1 ? \"\" : \"s\",","+                 boot == PARTITION_XBOOTLDR ? \"XBOOTLDR partition\" : \"ESP\", arg_image);","+        return 0;","+}","+"," static int parse_argv(int argc, char *argv[]) {","         assert(argc >= 0);","         assert(argv);","@@ -1448,6 +1709,23 @@ static int parse_argv(int argc, char *argv[]) {","                                 return r;","                         break;"," ","+                OPTION_LONG(\"addon\", \"NAME\", \"Write settings as PE addon into the boot partition of the image\"):","+                        /* The name becomes a file name on a FAT file system, which mtools has its own","+                         * ideas about, hence be as strict as for boot loader entries */","+                        if (!efi_loader_entry_name_valid(opts.arg))","+                                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Invalid addon name: %s\", opts.arg);","+","+                        r = free_and_strdup_warn(&arg_addon, opts.arg);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return r;","+                        break;","+","+                OPTION_LONG(\"key\", \"KEYRING:[NAME=]PATH\", \"Provision a certificate for a kernel keyring via the addon\"):","+                        r = parse_key_argument(opts.arg);","+                        if (r < 0)","+                                return r;","+                        break;","+","                 OPTION_LONG(\"force\", NULL, \"Overwrite existing files\"):","                         arg_force = true;","                         break;","@@ -1479,12 +1757,20 @@ static int parse_argv(int argc, char *argv[]) {","                 OPTION_GROUP(\"Settings\"): {}"," ","                 OPTION_LONG(\"locale\", \"LOCALE\", \"Set primary locale (LANG=)\"):","+                        if (!locale_is_valid(opts.arg))","+                                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL),","+                                                       \"Locale %s is not valid.\", opts.arg);","+","                         r = free_and_strdup_warn(&arg_locale, opts.arg);","                         if (r < 0)","                                 return r;","                         break;"," ","                 OPTION_LONG(\"locale-messages\", \"LOCALE\", \"Set message locale (LC_MESSAGES=)\"):","+                        if (!locale_is_valid(opts.arg))","+                                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL),","+                                                       \"Locale %s is not valid.\", opts.arg);","+","                         r = free_and_strdup_warn(&arg_locale_messages, opts.arg);","                         if (r < 0)","                                 return r;","@@ -1571,6 +1857,10 @@ static int parse_argv(int argc, char *argv[]) {","                         break;"," ","                 OPTION_LONG(\"root-shell\", \"SHELL\", \"Set root shell\"):","+                        if (!valid_shell(opts.arg))","+                                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL)